(*
# NpcDefinition
Decoder for the NPC definitions in index 2 (CONFIGS), archive 9 (`EConfigType.NPC`).
A straight port of `NpcLoader.java:52-431`, with `NpcDefinition.java` for the
defaults.

Only four of these fields reach the asset tree today - `SimbaNPCDumper` +
`NpcExporter.simbaExport` write `{name, level, category, minimapdot, actions,
size, colors}` per id - but the whole definition is decoded because the format is
a single stream: skipping a field means reading every field after it at the wrong
offset. Everything the client stores is therefore kept, not just what the current
dumper emits.

## Two opcodes the reference loader does not know
The live cache is newer than `runelite-cache`, whose `NpcLoader` warns and
continues on an opcode it does not recognise. Four NPCs (4733 "Thurgo" among
them) carry **opcode 147**, which that loader drops on the floor. Upstream
RuneLite (1.12.18-SNAPSHOT, 2026-02-11) has it - `def.zbuf = false` - along with
**opcode 130**, `def.idleAnimRestart = true`. Both are zero-byte flags, so the
reference loader stays aligned despite not knowing them, and both are decoded
here. Opcode 130 does not occur in the NPC archive of the cache this was written
against; it is implemented anyway, from the same upstream source.

Note that upstream and the `runelite-cache` fork in this workspace have diverged
in both directions: upstream has 130/147, the fork has 61/62 (32-bit model ids),
251/252/253 (the `TEntityOps` opcodes) and the type-2 int64 parameter. This port
is the union, which is what the cache actually contains.

## Coverage
Nine implemented opcodes are absent from all 15712 definitions in the cache this
was written against - **1, 60** (16-bit model / chathead ids, superseded by
61/62, which every npc uses), **116, 126, 129, 130, 251, 252, 253**. They are
implemented from the Java and pinned with synthetic definitions in
`dev/tests/250_npc.simba` rather than by real data. Two more are all but absent:
opcode 41 has exactly one user (npc 2702) and opcode 102 has 77, none of which
sets more than one head-icon bit - so the unset-bit branch of 102 is synthetic
too. Since 126 never appears, `FootprintSize` is in practice always the post
step's computed value.

## Revision assumptions
The Java loader carries two revision switches and this port hardcodes both to
their defaults, which is what `SimbaNPCDumper` uses (it never calls
`configureForRevision`):

- `rev210HeadIcons = true` (cache revision >= 1493, `REV_210_NPC_ARCHIVE_REV`).
  Opcode 102 is the bitfield form. The older form - a single u16 sprite index
  paired with the loader's `defaultHeadIconArchive` - is not implemented; a
  pre-1493 cache would decode it as a bitfield and desynchronise.
- `rev233 = true`. Opcode 111 therefore means `RenderPriority := 2`. Before 220
  the same opcode meant `IsFollower := True` plus `LowPriorityFollowerOps := True`;
  neither byte-consuming, so this only changes the values, never the alignment.

## Divergences from the Java
- An **unrecognised opcode raises**. `NpcLoader.decodeValues` logs a warning and
  returns, which leaves the stream parked mid-field and turns one unknown byte
  into a silently corrupt definition (and, because the loop runs to opcode 0, an
  arbitrary number of corrupt ones after it). Failing loudly is the only way a
  new opcode in a future cache revision gets noticed.
- **The stream must be exactly consumed.** After the terminating `0` the cursor
  has to sit at end-of-data; the Java never looks. A mis-sized opcode is
  otherwise invisible on the many definitions where the damaged field still
  decodes to something plausible, and not one of the 15712 NPCs in the archive
  leaves a trailing byte, so this is an always-on parity check rather than a
  heuristic. Same guard as `item.simba` and `object.simba`.

## Types
`Recolor*` and `Retexture*` hold **signed** 16-bit values: Java's arrays are
`short[]` and the loader casts the u16 it read, so 0x8000..0xFFFF come back
negative. That sign is preserved here rather than normalised, so the values match
`ModelDefinition.faceColors` (also `short`) that a recolour pass compares them
against. `HeadIconSpriteIndex` is a `short[]` in Java too, but its source
(`ReadUShortSmartMinusOne`) only spans -1..32766, so no value ever wraps.

Records with dynamic-array fields alias those arrays when copied (see
`TEntityOps`), so use one `TNpcDefinition` per definition and never copy one and
mutate the copy. `Load` calls `Default` itself, so every load gets fresh arrays.
*)
{$DEFINE WL_CACHE_DEF_NPC_INCLUDED}
{$IFNDEF WL_CACHE_BYTESTREAM_INCLUDED}{$INCLUDE_ONCE ../bytestream.simba}{$ENDIF}
{$IFNDEF WL_CACHE_ENTITYOPS_INCLUDED}{$INCLUDE_ONCE entityops.simba}{$ENDIF}

const
  // NpcDefinition.stats is a fixed 6-slot array filled by opcodes 74..79.
  NPC_STAT_COUNT: Integer = 6;

type
  TNpcDefinition = record
    Id: Integer;
    Name: String;
    Size: Integer;
    Models, ChatheadModels: TIntegerArray;

    StandingAnimation, WalkingAnimation: Integer;
    IdleRotateLeftAnimation, IdleRotateRightAnimation: Integer;
    Rotate180Animation, RotateLeftAnimation, RotateRightAnimation: Integer;
    RunAnimation, RunRotate180Animation: Integer;
    RunRotateLeftAnimation, RunRotateRightAnimation: Integer;
    CrawlAnimation, CrawlRotate180Animation: Integer;
    CrawlRotateLeftAnimation, CrawlRotateRightAnimation: Integer;

    RecolorToFind, RecolorToReplace: TIntegerArray;
    RetextureToFind, RetextureToReplace: TIntegerArray;

    Ops: TEntityOps;
    Params: TCacheParams;

    Category: Integer;
    CombatLevel: Integer;
    Stats: TIntegerArray;

    WidthScale, HeightScale, Height: Integer;
    RenderPriority, Ambient, Contrast, RotationSpeed: Integer;
    FootprintSize, OverlapTintHSL: Integer;

    HeadIconArchiveIds, HeadIconSpriteIndex: TIntegerArray;
    Configs: TIntegerArray;
    VarbitId, VarpIndex: Integer;

    IsMinimapVisible, IsInteractable, RotationFlag: Boolean;
    IsFollower, LowPriorityFollowerOps: Boolean;
    CanHideForOverlap, Unknown1, IdleAnimRestart: Boolean;
    // Note the inverted sense: opcode 147 clears this, it does not set it.
    Zbuf: Boolean;
  end;

(*
## TNpcDefinition.Default
```pascal
function TNpcDefinition.Default(id: Integer): TNpcDefinition; static;
```
Every field at the value `NpcDefinition.java` gives it before any opcode runs.
The non-obvious ones: `Name` is the literal string `'null'` (not empty),
`RotationSpeed` is 32, `OverlapTintHSL` is 39188, `Category` is 0 (not -1 - it is
a plain `int` field with no initialiser in the Java) and `FootprintSize` starts at
-1 as the sentinel `Load`'s post step tests for.
*)
function TNpcDefinition.Default(id: Integer): TNpcDefinition; static;
var
  i: Integer;
begin
  Result.Id := id;
  Result.Name := 'null';
  Result.Size := 1;

  Result.StandingAnimation := -1;
  Result.WalkingAnimation := -1;
  Result.IdleRotateLeftAnimation := -1;
  Result.IdleRotateRightAnimation := -1;
  Result.Rotate180Animation := -1;
  Result.RotateLeftAnimation := -1;
  Result.RotateRightAnimation := -1;
  Result.RunAnimation := -1;
  Result.RunRotate180Animation := -1;
  Result.RunRotateLeftAnimation := -1;
  Result.RunRotateRightAnimation := -1;
  Result.CrawlAnimation := -1;
  Result.CrawlRotate180Animation := -1;
  Result.CrawlRotateLeftAnimation := -1;
  Result.CrawlRotateRightAnimation := -1;

  Result.Ops := TEntityOps.Create();

  Result.CombatLevel := -1;
  Result.WidthScale := 128;
  Result.HeightScale := 128;
  Result.RotationSpeed := 32;
  Result.VarbitId := -1;
  Result.VarpIndex := -1;
  Result.Height := -1;
  Result.FootprintSize := -1;
  Result.OverlapTintHSL := 39188;

  Result.IsMinimapVisible := True;
  Result.IsInteractable := True;
  Result.RotationFlag := True;
  Result.Zbuf := True;

  SetLength(Result.Stats, NPC_STAT_COUNT);
  for i := 0 to NPC_STAT_COUNT - 1 do
    Result.Stats[i] := 1;
end;

(*
## TNpcDefinition.Load
```pascal
function TNpcDefinition.Load(id: Integer; data: TByteArray): TNpcDefinition; static;
```
Decodes one NPC definition. `data` is a single file out of
`TCacheStore.ReadFiles(2, Ord(EConfigType.NPC), [])`, and `id` is the matching
entry of the reference table's `FileIds` - not the array position, though for the
NPC archive the two happen to coincide today.

Reads opcodes until the 0 terminator, then applies the post step from
`NpcLoader.post`: an unset `FootprintSize` becomes `0.4 * Size * 128` truncated.
The Java does that in **float**, this in double, and the two agree for every
`Size` a u8 can hold - 0.4 rounds up in both, so the product sits a fraction of
an ulp above the exact 51.2 * `Size` and truncates the same way. The exact form
is `(Size * 256) div 5`; `dev/tests/250_npc.simba` pins the identity over 0..255.

Raises on an opcode the loader does not know, and again if the definition does
not end exactly on its terminator - both name the npc id and the byte offset.
*)
function TNpcDefinition.Load(id: Integer; data: TByteArray): TNpcDefinition; static;
var
  s: TByteStream;
  opcode, n, i, bitfield, bits, extra: Integer;
begin
  Result := TNpcDefinition.Default(id);
  s := TByteStream.Create(data);

  while True do
  begin
    opcode := s.ReadUByte();
    if opcode = 0 then Break;

    case opcode of
      1: begin
           n := s.ReadUByte();
           SetLength(Result.Models, n);
           for i := 0 to n - 1 do
             Result.Models[i] := s.ReadUShort();
         end;

      2: Result.Name := s.ReadJagexString();

      12: Result.Size := s.ReadUByte();
      13: Result.StandingAnimation := s.ReadUShort();
      14: Result.WalkingAnimation := s.ReadUShort();
      15: Result.IdleRotateLeftAnimation := s.ReadUShort();
      16: Result.IdleRotateRightAnimation := s.ReadUShort();

      17: begin
            Result.WalkingAnimation := s.ReadUShort();
            Result.Rotate180Animation := s.ReadUShort();
            Result.RotateLeftAnimation := s.ReadUShort();
            Result.RotateRightAnimation := s.ReadUShort();
          end;

      18: Result.Category := s.ReadUShort();

      30..34: Result.Ops.DecodeOp(s, opcode - 30);

      // Java stores these as short[], so a u16 over 32767 comes back negative.
      40: begin
            n := s.ReadUByte();
            SetLength(Result.RecolorToFind, n);
            SetLength(Result.RecolorToReplace, n);
            for i := 0 to n - 1 do
            begin
              Result.RecolorToFind[i] := s.ReadShort();
              Result.RecolorToReplace[i] := s.ReadShort();
            end;
          end;

      41: begin
            n := s.ReadUByte();
            SetLength(Result.RetextureToFind, n);
            SetLength(Result.RetextureToReplace, n);
            for i := 0 to n - 1 do
            begin
              Result.RetextureToFind[i] := s.ReadShort();
              Result.RetextureToReplace[i] := s.ReadShort();
            end;
          end;

      60: begin
            n := s.ReadUByte();
            SetLength(Result.ChatheadModels, n);
            for i := 0 to n - 1 do
              Result.ChatheadModels[i] := s.ReadUShort();
          end;

      // 61/62 are 1/60 with 32-bit model ids.
      61: begin
            n := s.ReadUByte();
            SetLength(Result.Models, n);
            for i := 0 to n - 1 do
              Result.Models[i] := s.ReadInt();
          end;

      62: begin
            n := s.ReadUByte();
            SetLength(Result.ChatheadModels, n);
            for i := 0 to n - 1 do
              Result.ChatheadModels[i] := s.ReadInt();
          end;

      74..79: Result.Stats[opcode - 74] := s.ReadUShort();

      93: Result.IsMinimapVisible := False;
      95: Result.CombatLevel := s.ReadUShort();
      97: Result.WidthScale := s.ReadUShort();
      98: Result.HeightScale := s.ReadUShort();
      99: Result.RenderPriority := 1;

      100: Result.Ambient := s.ReadByte();
      // Stored RAW, matching the cache byte, RuneLite's NpcLoader, and the
      // committed npcs.zip - same convention as TItemDefinition.Contrast.
      //
      // A renderer MUST scale it by 5 first. Decompiled client:
      // LostCityRS/OS1 NpcType.java:241 `this.contrast = buf.g1b() * 5`,
      // consumed at :317 as `light(ambient + 64, contrast + 850, -30, -50, -30)`
      // - note NPCs use +850 and light vector (-30,-50,-30), where items use
      // +768 and (-50,-10,-50). See docs/phase2-render-spec.md.
      101: Result.Contrast := s.ReadByte();

      // Head icons (prayer/skull overlays), one slot per set bit of a u8
      // bitfield. `bits` is the bitfield's bit *length*, so the trailing zero
      // bits below the highest set one still get a slot - filled with -1/-1 and
      // consuming nothing.
      102: begin
             bitfield := s.ReadUByte();
             bits := 0;
             i := bitfield;
             while i <> 0 do
             begin
               Inc(bits);
               i := i shr 1;
             end;

             SetLength(Result.HeadIconArchiveIds, bits);
             SetLength(Result.HeadIconSpriteIndex, bits);
             for i := 0 to bits - 1 do
               if (bitfield and (1 shl i)) = 0 then
               begin
                 Result.HeadIconArchiveIds[i] := -1;
                 Result.HeadIconSpriteIndex[i] := -1;
               end
               else
               begin
                 Result.HeadIconArchiveIds[i] := s.ReadBigSmart2();
                 Result.HeadIconSpriteIndex[i] := s.ReadUShortSmartMinusOne();
               end;
           end;

      103: Result.RotationSpeed := s.ReadUShort();

      // 106 and 118 differ only in the last Configs slot: -1 versus the extra
      // u16 that 118 reads up front. Both size the array n + 2 and fill n + 1.
      106, 118: begin
                  Result.VarbitId := s.ReadUShort();
                  if Result.VarbitId = 65535 then Result.VarbitId := -1;

                  Result.VarpIndex := s.ReadUShort();
                  if Result.VarpIndex = 65535 then Result.VarpIndex := -1;

                  extra := -1;
                  if opcode = 118 then
                  begin
                    extra := s.ReadUShort();
                    if extra = 65535 then extra := -1;
                  end;

                  n := s.ReadUByte();
                  SetLength(Result.Configs, n + 2);
                  for i := 0 to n do
                  begin
                    Result.Configs[i] := s.ReadUShort();
                    if Result.Configs[i] = 65535 then Result.Configs[i] := -1;
                  end;
                  Result.Configs[n + 1] := extra;
                end;

      107: Result.IsInteractable := False;
      109: Result.RotationFlag := False;
      // rev233; before 220 this was IsFollower + LowPriorityFollowerOps.
      111: Result.RenderPriority := 2;

      114: Result.RunAnimation := s.ReadUShort();
      115: begin
             Result.RunAnimation := s.ReadUShort();
             Result.RunRotate180Animation := s.ReadUShort();
             Result.RunRotateLeftAnimation := s.ReadUShort();
             Result.RunRotateRightAnimation := s.ReadUShort();
           end;

      116: Result.CrawlAnimation := s.ReadUShort();
      117: begin
             Result.CrawlAnimation := s.ReadUShort();
             Result.CrawlRotate180Animation := s.ReadUShort();
             Result.CrawlRotateLeftAnimation := s.ReadUShort();
             Result.CrawlRotateRightAnimation := s.ReadUShort();
           end;

      122: Result.IsFollower := True;
      123: Result.LowPriorityFollowerOps := True;
      124: Result.Height := s.ReadUShort();
      126: Result.FootprintSize := s.ReadUShort();
      129: Result.Unknown1 := True;
      // 130 and 147 are upstream-only, see the unit docstring.
      130: Result.IdleAnimRestart := True;
      145: Result.CanHideForOverlap := True;
      146: Result.OverlapTintHSL := s.ReadUShort();
      147: Result.Zbuf := False;

      249: Result.Params := s.ReadParams();

      251: Result.Ops.DecodeSubOp(s);
      252: Result.Ops.DecodeConditionalOp(s);
      253: Result.Ops.DecodeConditionalSubOp(s);

      else
        raise 'NpcDefinition: unknown opcode ' + ToStr(opcode) + ' for npc ' +
              ToStr(id) + ' at offset ' + ToStr(s.Position - 1);
    end;
  end;

  if s.Remaining() <> 0 then
    raise 'NpcDefinition: npc ' + ToStr(id) + ' left ' + ToStr(s.Remaining()) +
          ' byte(s) unread after its terminator at offset ' + ToStr(s.Position - 1);

  // post - NpcLoader.java:73-79.
  if Result.FootprintSize = -1 then
    Result.FootprintSize := Trunc(0.4 * (Result.Size * 128));
end;
